  <middle>
    <section anchor="overview" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-1">
      <name slugifiedName="name-overview">Overview</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1">The Real-time Transport Protocol (RTP) provides end-to-end network
transport functions suitable for applications transmitting real-time
data such as audio or video over multicast or unicast network
services.  The data transport is augmented by the RTP Control
Protocol (RTCP) to allow monitoring of the data delivery in a manner
scalable to large multicast networks and to provide minimal control
and identification functionality.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-2">&quot;SDP: Session Description Protocol&quot; <xref target="RFC4566" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4566"/> provides a general-purpose
format for describing multimedia sessions in announcements or
invitations.  &quot;TCP-Based Media Transport in the Session Description
Protocol (SDP)&quot; <xref target="RFC4145" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4145"/> specifies a general mechanism for
describing media transport over TCP using SDP with <xref target="RFC4571" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4571"/> defining
a method for framing RTP and RTCP packets <xref target="RFC3550" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC3550"/> onto a
connection-oriented transport (such as TCP).  &quot;Connection-Oriented
Media Transport over the Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol in
the Session Description Protocol (SDP)&quot; <xref target="RFC4572" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4572"/> extends <xref target="RFC4145" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4145"/>
for describing TCP-based media streams that are protected using TLS
<xref target="RFC5246" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5246"/>.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-3">This specification describes additional SDP transport protocol
identifiers for transporting RTP media over TCP as defined in
<xref target="section-3" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="Section 3"/>.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="terminology" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2">
      <name slugifiedName="name-terminology">Terminology</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-2-1">The key words &quot;<bcp14>MUST</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>MUST NOT</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>REQUIRED</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHALL</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHALL NOT</bcp14>&quot;,
&quot;<bcp14>SHOULD</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHOULD NOT</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>RECOMMENDED</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>MAY</bcp14>&quot;, and &quot;<bcp14>OPTIONAL</bcp14>&quot; in this
document are to be interpreted as described in RFC 2119 <xref target="RFC2119" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC2119"/>.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="protocol-identifiers" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3">
      <name slugifiedName="name-protocol-identifiers">Protocol Identifiers</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-1">The &quot;m=&quot; line in SDP specifies, among other items, the transport
protocol (identified via the &quot;proto&quot; field) to be used for the media
in the session.  See Section 5.14 (Media Descriptions) of SDP
<xref target="RFC4566" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4566"/> for a discussion on transport protocol identifiers.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-2">The following is the format for an &quot;m=&quot; line, as specified in
<xref target="RFC4566" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4566"/>:</t>
      <artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt="" pn="section-3-3"><![CDATA[
          m=<media> <port> <proto> <fmt> ...
]]></artwork>
      <section anchor="tcp/rtp/avpf-transport-realization" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3.1">
        <name slugifiedName="name-tcp/rtp/avpf-transport-realization">TCP/RTP/AVPF Transport Realization</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.1-1">The TCP/RTP/AVPF transport describes RTP media with RTCP-based
feedback <xref target="RFC4585" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4585"/> over TCP.</t>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.1-2">The RTP/AVPF stream over TCP is realized using the framing method
defined in <xref target="RFC4571" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4571"/>.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="tcp/rtp/savp-transport-realization" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3.2">
        <name slugifiedName="name-tcp/rtp/savp-transport-realization">TCP/RTP/SAVP Transport Realization</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.2-1">The TCP/RTP/SAVP transport describes Secure RTP (SRTP) media
<xref target="RFC3711" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC3711"/> over TCP.</t>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.2-2">The RTP/SAVP stream over TCP is realized using the framing method
defined in <xref target="RFC4571" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4571"/>.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="tcp/rtp/savpf-transport-realization" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3.3">
        <name slugifiedName="name-tcp/rtp/savpf-transport-realization">TCP/RTP/SAVPF Transport Realization</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.3-1">The TCP/RTP/SAVPF transport describes Secure RTP media with RTCP-based
feedback <xref target="RFC5124" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5124"/> over TCP.</t>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.3-2">The RTP/SAVPF stream over TCP is realized using the framing method
defined in <xref target="RFC4571" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4571"/>.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="tcp/dtls/rtp/savp-transport-realization" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3.4">
        <name slugifiedName="name-tcp/dtls/rtp/savp-transport-realization">TCP/DTLS/RTP/SAVP Transport Realization</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.4-1">The TCP/DTLS/RTP/SAVP transport describes Secure RTP media <xref target="RFC3711" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC3711"/>
using Datagram Transport Layer Security SRTP (DTLS-SRTP) <xref target="RFC5764" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5764"/>
over TCP.</t>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.4-2">RTP/SAVP using DTLS-based key establishment is realized according to
the procedures defined in <xref target="RFC5764" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5764"/>.  Also, the framing specified in
<xref target="RFC4571" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4571"/> is used to transport DTLS-SRTP packets over TCP.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="tcp/dtls/rtp/savpf-transport-realization" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3.5">
        <name slugifiedName="name-tcp/dtls/rtp/savpf-transport-realization">TCP/DTLS/RTP/SAVPF Transport Realization</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.5-1">The TCP/DTLS/RTP/SAVPF transport describes Secure RTP media with
RTCP-based feedback <xref target="RFC5124" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5124"/> using DTLS-SRTP over TCP.</t>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.5-2">RTP/SAVPF using DTLS-based key establishment is realized according to
the procedures defined in <xref target="RFC5764" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5764"/>.  Also, the framing specified in
<xref target="RFC4571" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4571"/> is used to transport DTLS-SRTP packets over TCP.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="tcp/tls/rtp/avp-transport-realization" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3.6">
        <name slugifiedName="name-tcp/tls/rtp/avp-transport-realization">TCP/TLS/RTP/AVP Transport Realization</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.6-1">The TCP/TLS/RTP/AVP transport describes RTP Media on top of TLS over
TCP.</t>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.6-2">RTP/AVP packets are framed using the procedures from <xref target="RFC4571" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4571"/> and
are transported as application data messages over the TLS association
setup using the procedures from <xref target="RFC4572" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4572"/>.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="tcp/tls/rtp/avpf-transport-realization" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3.7">
        <name slugifiedName="name-tcp/tls/rtp/avpf-transport-realization">TCP/TLS/RTP/AVPF Transport Realization</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.7-1">The TCP/TLS/RTP/AVPF transport describes RTP media with RTCP-based
feedback <xref target="RFC5124" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5124"/> on top of TLS over TCP.</t>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.7-2">RTP/AVPF packets are framed using the procedures from <xref target="RFC4571" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4571"/> and
are transported as application data messages over the TLS association
setup using the procedures from <xref target="RFC4572" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4572"/>.</t>
      </section>
    </section>
    <section anchor="ice-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4">
      <name slugifiedName="name-ice-considerations">ICE Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-4-1">When procedures from <xref target="RFC6544" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6544"/> are used to set up Interactive
Connectivity Establishment (ICE) <xref target="RFC5245" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5245"/> candidates for a TCP
transport, the framing mechanism from <xref target="RFC4571" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4571"/> <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> be used for
framing Session Traversal Utilities for NAT (STUN) packets (for
keepalives and consent checks), as defined in <xref target="RFC6544" section="3" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6544#section-3" derivedContent="RFC6544"/>.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="iana-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-5">
      <name slugifiedName="name-iana-considerations">IANA Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-5-1">This specification describes the following new SDP transport protocol
identifiers: 'TCP/RTP/AVPF', 'TCP/RTP/SAVP', 'TCP/RTP/SAVPF',
'TCP/DTLS/RTP/SAVP', 'TCP/DTLS/RTP/SAVPF', 'TCP/TLS/RTP/AVP', and
'TCP/TLS/RTP/AVPF', as defined in <xref target="section-3" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="Section 3"/>.  These values have been
registered by the IANA under the &quot;proto&quot; subregistry in the &quot;Session
Description Protocol (SDP) Parameters&quot; registry.</t>
