    <section anchor="security-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-6">
      <name slugifiedName="name-security-considerations">Security Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-6-1">The new &quot;proto&quot; identifiers registered by this document in the SDP
parameters registry maintained by IANA are primarily for use by the
offer/answer model of the Session Description Protocol <xref target="RFC3264" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC3264"/> for
the negotiation and establishment of RTP-based media over the TCP
transport.  This specification doesn't introduce any additional
security considerations beyond those specified by the individual
transport protocols identified in the &quot;proto&quot; identifiers and those
detailed in <xref target="RFC4566" section="7" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4566#section-7" derivedContent="RFC4566"/>.</t>
    </section>
